N2  - The proceedings contain 49 papers. The topics discussed include: correction of vitamin d deficiency in critically ill patients: a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled pilot study; exceptional bone mineral density gain over 6 years attributable to permanent hypoparathyroidism after thyroidectomy in a 36-year-old woman; increased physical activity is associated with favourable body composition and higher bone density; association between bone mineral density and coronary atherosclerosis in patients with Type-2 diabetes; assessment of fatty liver index (FLI) in relation to insulin sensitivity in women with prior gestational diabetes; Type-2 diabetes mellitus is a common complication following cardiac transplantation: does developing glycemia prevent catch-up in bone mineral density?; and thyroid stimulating hormone-secreting pituitary adenoma: a rare, diagnostically challenging, and potentially curable disease.
